{"term":"velvet","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4b5cb66ca882bc5c08","definition":"A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","example":"For the first time since her husband's death, she had thrown off her weeds, and put on attire more suited to the occasion. She was richly, yet plainly dressed, in a purple velvet, with a hood of white point lace. Even her silent handmaids were surprised out of their ordinary propriety by her appearance.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beggars' velvet","black velvet","cotton velvet","crushed velvet","Florida velvet bean","on velvet","pink velvet cake","poor man's black velvet","purple velvet plant","red velvet","red-velvet cake","red velvet cake","red velvet mite","slashed velvet","stand on velvet","tip someone's velvet","Utrecht velvet","velveret","velvet ant","velvet antler","velvet ash","velvet bean","velvetbreast","velvet cichlid","velvet cork","velvet crab","velvet divorce","velvet duck","velveteen","velvetfish"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1cfaf2df6196f3052f","definition":"Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers.","example":"His [a hart's] head when it commeth firſt out, hath a ruſſet pyll vpon it, the which is called Veluet, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["beggars' velvet","black velvet","cotton velvet","crushed velvet","Florida velvet bean","on velvet","pink velvet cake","poor man's black velvet","purple velvet plant","red velvet","red-velvet cake","red velvet cake","red velvet mite","slashed velvet","stand on velvet","tip someone's velvet","Utrecht velvet","velveret","velvet ant","velvet ant